Subject: [PATCH 0021] Let the stream window be windowed or closed by the user

The stream window is now the thing the user looks at, so it has to behave like
one. F11 switches between the two modes that matter:

- Fullscreen is click-through. The interface window underneath keeps the input
  focus, so the game keeps receiving the clicks and keys that already travel
  through it, and the keyboard shortcut that toggles the mode still arrives.
- Windowed is a normal 1280x720 toplevel with a viewport scaling the decoder
  buffer. The compositor decorates it, so it can be moved, and its close button
  is reachable. Clicks now land on the window instead of the interface, which
  is exactly right while the game is not being played.

Closing the window ends the stream instead of leaving an invisible player
running: the surface reports the compositor's close request to the interface,
which stops the session the same way the in-stream menu does.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

